UNIT languages_of
KIND FUNCTIONAL
FIDELITY package
ANCHOR rederive@bb8ded84fa50 cli/features.mjs languagesOf — the fail-closed language gate (round 5); reproduce the code exactly, accidents included
ORACLE-CLASS deterministic
SIG languages_of(input: json) -> list[text]
ENVELOPE input is json. The domain is a map whose entry sirFiles (optional) is a list of text — SIR file names or paths —
  and whose entry variants (optional, or none) is a map from variant keys (package or lang:<id>) to maps, each with
  optional text entries lang and sir (sir naming a .sir file).
  Every other shape is OUT-OF-DOMAIN and throws (R1, R2, R5, R6). Throws are IN scope as observations: only throw-ness is
  graded, never the message. Text is Unicode scalar values; a lone surrogate is a js-only widening (see the js file).
DEPENDS-ON none
DESCRIPTION The target languages a SIR bundle carries, read from its structure only: the language segment of every SIR file
  name <unit>.<lang>.sir, every variants key lang:<id>, a variant's own lang entry and the language of its sir path. The gate
  fails closed: a malformed SIR name, an id outside the closed language registry, a variant whose names disagree or that
  names a language while pointing at a SIR that names none, two variants claiming one language, a variant key other than
  package or lang:<id>, a unit name outside the unit-name grammar, a variant sir that names no .sir file, or an argument of
  the wrong shape throws. The result lists each language once, sorted.
BEHAVIOR
R1 input is not a map (none, a list, text, a number or a bool) -> throws. Entries other than sirFiles and variants are ignored.
R2 FILES = the entry sirFiles: missing -> the empty list; a list -> its elements; anything else (none included) -> throws. An
  element that is not text -> throws.
R3 CLAIM-OF(path) is an id, nothing, or a throw. BASE = the part of path after its last "/" or "\" (all of path when it holds
  neither), with SPACE-TAB characters removed from both ends (only those). A SIR-END is the four characters "." then one of
  SIR-CASE's s S, one of i I, one of r R — an ASCII-only fold.
  (a) BASE is text that ends with a SIR-END, followed by one or more HIDDEN characters to the very end -> throws.
  (b) Otherwise, BASE not ending with a SIR-END -> nothing (x.ts.sir.bak, x.ts.sir~, x.ts.sir/, README.md, x.ts.ſir, x.ts.sır).
  (c) Otherwise STEM = BASE without its last four characters, cut at every "." into SEGMENTS; UNIT = the first SEGMENT.
  UNIT not empty and not a UNIT-NAME -> throws (x y.ts.sir, é.sir, -x.ts.sir, a<LF>b.rust.sir; an empty UNIT is allowed).
  More than two SEGMENTS -> throws (a.b.ts.sir, x.go.ts.sir, ...sir). One SEGMENT -> nothing (x.sir, .sir, ts.sir). Two: the
  second empty -> throws (x..sir, ..sir); else the claim is the second exactly as written, no case change or trim (.php.sir
  claims php; a.b.sir claims b, which R4 refuses).
R4 SIGHT(id): id not in REGISTRY (exact, case-sensitive) -> throws; otherwise id is SIGHTED. Each element of FILES with a
  claim is sighted: x.TS.sir, x.carried.sir and "x. ts.sir" throw.
R5 VARIANTS = the entry variants: missing or none -> no entries; a map -> its entries; anything else (a list, text, number or
  bool — false and 0 included) -> throws. Entry order is immaterial: every check below is per entry or over all entries.
R6 For each entry K -> V of VARIANTS:
  (a) V not a map -> throws. V has an entry lang that is not text (none included) -> throws. V has an entry sir that is not
  text -> throws. V has a text sir: CLAIM-OF(sir) is taken (it may throw, R3), and BASE of sir (as R3 cuts it) not ending
  with a SIR-END -> throws (the empty text, "/", README.md, x.ts.sir.bak, x.ts.sir/).
  (b) K is neither exactly package nor exactly lang: followed by a LANG-ID -> throws (Lang:ts, lang:, lang:TS, lang:1ts,
  " lang:ts", default, look-alikes with a Cyrillic letter, a fullwidth colon or an invisible character). The LANG-ID runs to
  the very end of K: lang:ts followed by a line feed throws.
  (c) KEYLANG = the LANG-ID of a lang: key (none for package); OWNLANG = V's lang (the empty text included); PATHLANG =
  CLAIM-OF(V's sir) when V has a sir. NAMED = those present.
  (d) two members of NAMED differ (exact comparison) -> throws.
  (e) KEYLANG or OWNLANG present, V has a sir, and PATHLANG is nothing -> throws (lang:ts, or package with lang ts, and sir x.sir).
  (f) NAMED empty -> the entry contributes nothing (only a package key without lang whose sir is absent or a one-SEGMENT name).
  (g) otherwise SIGHT(the one id NAMED holds) — so lang:go or an empty lang throws — and that id is claimed by K: two entries
  claiming one id -> throws. A FILES claim and a variant claim of the same id do not conflict.
R7 The result is the SIGHTED ids, each once, in ascending order (every REGISTRY id is ASCII lowercase, so any text order
  agrees). A throw anywhere is the outcome of the whole call: no partial result.
PINNED names REGISTRY = js ts rust php csharp python CITED capabilities.json toolchain.languageRegistry at the anchor commit — the closed registry
PINNED charset SPACE-TAB = U+0020 U+0009 CITED R3 — the only characters trimmed; NBSP, U+0085, U+FEFF stay and so reach R3(a)
PINNED charset VISIBLE = U+0021-U+007E CITED R3(a) — visible ASCII, the only characters that may follow a SIR-END without a throw
PINNED charset HIDDEN = every code point outside VISIBLE CITED R3(a) — space, controls, DEL, every non-ASCII code point whether visible, invisible, private-use or unassigned; a fixed set, never a Unicode table
PINNED chars SIR-CASE = s S i I r R CITED R3 — ASCII only: U+017F, U+0131 and U+0130 never stand for s or i
PINNED grammar UNIT-NAME = one of A-Z a-z 0-9 _ then zero or more of A-Z a-z 0-9 _ - (ASCII only), the whole UNIT CITED R3(c) FINDINGS #77
PINNED grammar LANG-ID = one of a-z then zero or more of a-z 0-9 (ASCII only), the whole rest of K CITED R6(b) FINDINGS #77 — lang:go passes the key grammar and R4 refuses it
INVARIANT the result is sorted, never holds a duplicate, and every member is in REGISTRY; the input is never modified.
OUT-OF-DOMAIN what the code does outside ENVELOPE, all reproduced: every shape violation throws.
  1. The input itself not a map throws (R1).
  2. sirFiles not a list, or an element not text, throws (R2). variants neither a map nor none throws (R5).
  3. A variant that is not a map, whose lang is not text, or whose sir is not text naming a .sir file, throws (R6a); a
  variant key outside package / lang:<id> throws (R6b).
ORACLE value -> oracles/languages_of.json  CANONICAL-SHA256 8c9d31d3992f56852ec43f596bc0160638d27cdb9aa1dbdbabb81a93547bfed9
SCOPE IN: R1–R7, OUT-OF-DOMAIN 1–3. OUT: deciding what the languages mean (harnessing, toolchains) — the caller's job.
PROVENANCE rederive@bb8ded84fa50 cli/features.mjs (languagesOf, langOfPath, SIR_TAIL, HIDDEN_TAIL) and cli/capabilities.json
  (toolchain.languageRegistry), MIT. Round 5 (2026-10-27, REDERIVE_SELF_PLAN Tier 1) against the fixed gate (FINDINGS #77),
  through seams/languages_of.mjs (the returned set listed in iteration order, which the code sorts).
